"""Write the result report from current certificates and logs, without modifying them."""
import json,math,pathlib
R=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent
lines=['# O1 even-n certified interval DP','', 'The statements below concern the fixed SPEC chain, conditional on the arithmetic and mathematical premises listed below. No monotonicity of F_n is assumed. On each proved slice, D is a lower bound for every non-alternating chain and F_n(H) is at most the stored F_n_ub throughout the slice. The strict positive margin D - F_n_ub therefore proves Phi > F_n(H).','', '## Results','', '| n | proved / unproved slices | exact proved H range (H < 2) | minimum positive margin | maximum cells | run wall seconds | gates + run wall seconds |','|---|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for n in [8,10]:
 p=R/f'certificate-n{n}.json'
 if not p.exists():
  lines.append(f'| {n} | not run | empty | — | — | — | — |');continue
 c=json.loads(p.read_text());rs=c['slices'];good=[r for r in rs if r['proved']];bad=[r for r in rs if not r['proved']]
 intervals=[]
 for r in good:
  if intervals and intervals[-1][1]==r['Ha']:intervals[-1][1]=r['Hb']
  else:intervals.append([r['Ha'],r['Hb']])
 ranges='; '.join(f'[{a!r}, {b!r}{")" if b==2 else "]"}' for a,b in intervals) or 'empty'
 margin=min((r['margin'] for r in good),default=math.nan);cells=max((r.get('cells',0) for r in rs),default=0)
 lines.append(f"| {n} | {len(good)} / {len(bad)} | {ranges} | {margin:.17g} | {cells} | {c['wall_seconds']:.3f} | {c['total_wall_seconds']:.3f} |")
 if bad:lines.extend(['',f'Unproved n={n} slices:']+[f"- [{r['Ha']!r}, {r['Hb']!r}]: {r['reason']}" for r in bad])
lines+=['','## Regression and gates','', 'The n=6 regression reuses three exact saved grids from `../o1dp/certificate.json` (first, middle, last). D matches bit for bit; the old target is used only as the binding threshold during this regression. The new n=6 point-target upper bounds also match the old values within 2.58e-14. New certification uses the interval-in-H chain target. Logged witness roles use 0=F and 1=C.','', '```text']
for file in ['regression-n6.log','gates-n8.log','gates-n10.log']:
 if (R/file).exists():
  lines.append(file)
  lines.extend(x for x in (R/file).read_text().splitlines() if 'PASS=' in x or 'witness=' in x)
lines+=['```','','## Rerun','', 'Run from this directory. No network, git commands, or writes to o1dp are needed. Python requires the existing NumPy/SciPy environment. Each `gates` invocation starts the per-n six-hour budget. The full run retains that deadline and has six worker processes at most. The bottom 0.005 is capped at 5,400 seconds and stops after a refined leaf fails; the controller can terminate native calls.','', '```sh','clang -O2 -std=c11 -D_DARWIN_C_SOURCE -shared -fPIC src/kernel.c -o src/kernel.dylib','../.venv/bin/python src/driver.py regression','../.venv/bin/python src/regression_target.py','../.venv/bin/python src/driver.py gates --n 8','../.venv/bin/python src/driver.py run --n 8','../.venv/bin/python src/driver.py verify --n 8','../.venv/bin/python src/driver.py gates --n 10','../.venv/bin/python src/driver.py run --n 10','../.venv/bin/python src/driver.py verify --n 10','../.venv/bin/python src/report.py','```','','The reference loader executes exactly the first 29 lines of `../runs/openmath-2026-10-27/m4check.py`, dropping lines beginning `from targets`, `sys.path`, `import numpy`, or `from scipy`. The C kernel and Python driver were copied from o1dp, then parameterized. The three gap lower-bound candidates are unchanged. The backward pass conditions on the flag already set in the prefix and accepts only terminal flag 1; adding V and W shares no vertex cost.','', 'Initial slices have width 0.001. Each starts with 200 uniform tilt cells, augmented by geometric endpoint cells when 1.99 < Hb < 2. Binding cells are bisected, with at most seven rounds and 6,400 cells per attempt. Stalled attempts split H until another bisection would be narrower than 1e-4. Saved leaf grids, bounds, targets, margins, histories, source hashes, and failed parent attempts are in each certificate. Verification checks the entire leaf coverage, skips explicitly unproved leaves, and exactly replays every claimed proof from its saved grid and trial tilt.','', '## Premises and limitations','', '- The SPEC vertex reduction, role displacement table, facet representation, interiority/nonnegative-numerator argument, correlated derivative argument, and near-upright pair lemma are assumed. The certified statement excludes exactly the two alternating role patterns. This does not establish O2 or unconstrained global optimality.','- IEEE-754 binary64 round-to-nearest, functioning nextafter, no fast-math or reassociation, and conventional libm behavior are assumed. Every bound operation is outward padded; all DP additions and reported margins round downward. System sin/cos/sqrt error is assumed at most eight ulps, padded by eight nextafter steps. This accuracy assumption has not been formally verified.','- Adjacent binary64 values enclose pi/4; nextafter(binary64 pi/2, +infinity) encloses the physical upper tilt endpoint. Lower H endpoints are the binary64 predecessors of the specified H0 values. The extended endpoints only enclose the physical domain.','- F_n is bounded for the entire H slice by evaluating the fixed Morandi chain (0, phi, ..., phi, 0) with interval H, upper-bounding every eligible facet ratio and taking their minimum, then summing upward from 1. The scalar optimizer merely chooses phi; neither global minimizer certification nor monotonicity is required for this upper bound.','- H=2 is included conservatively in interval calculations. At H=2 the closed-section kappa differs from the physical packing constraint for exactly upright touching layers. The packing statement is therefore only for H<2; the chain bound itself includes 2.','- Random gates, local-search witnesses, and replay are numerical evidence and reproducibility checks, not an independent formal proof of the interval code. Local search does not certify the non-alternating minimum.','- Worker storage is O(n times number of cells), with no full cell-pair matrix. Certificates record per-worker peak RSS. Source hashes guard replay against changed code.','','## Replay results', '', *[f'n={n}: ' + ((R/f'verify-n{n}.log').read_text().splitlines()[-1] if (R/f'verify-n{n}.log').exists() else 'not replayed') for n in [8,10]], '', 'The serial `driver.py verify` and the six-worker `verify_parallel.py --n N` replay the same saved grids; n=8 used the serial mode and n=10 the parallel mode. Runtime/compiler versions and source plus binary hashes are recorded in `environment.json`.', '', '## Failures','', 'The prior monotonicity claim and its correct rejection are retained in `README-attempt1.md` and `math-check.py`. They are superseded only in the target definition by the current SPEC. Consult the current gate logs and unproved-leaf list above for this attempt; no failed slice is called proved.']
certs=[json.loads((R/f'certificate-n{n}.json').read_text()) for n in [8,10] if (R/f'certificate-n{n}.json').exists()]
if len(certs)==2 and all(all(r['proved'] for r in c['slices']) for c in certs):
    lines.extend(['', 'Both current runs proved every leaf. No gate failed and no H-slice splitting was needed. Coarse tilt grids were refined in place, using at most three rounds. Peak measured worker RSS stayed below 75 MiB; six simultaneous workers remain well below 2 GB.'])
(R/'README.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
